module unsigned_neg.neg_1

// ONE seeded cause: unary minus on an UNSIGNED operand -- the spec
// (conversions.md: "Unary minus is defined for signed types only") makes it a
// compile error, not a modular wrap. The oracle accepted this program and
// printed 56 for `-200u8` (registry #926) until f61183148 (registry 1547) gave
// it E_NEG_UNSIGNED. Wave 274.7 B4. The operand is a parameter because a typed
// local (`ro u u8 = 200`) is outside novac's subset today (E2-b3) and would be
// the refusal instead of the seeded one.
//
// THE CODE IS PINNED (2026-10-01): a language error, E_NOVAC_LANG, not the
// subset's E_NOVAC_SUBSET -- the refusal used to go out under the debt code,
// as if a later wave would compile it. The marker below pins the oracle's
// code in the text; pipeline/prims_test pins the diagnostic's own `code`.
// NOVAC_EXPECT unary minus is defined for signed types only (E_NEG_UNSIGNED
fn flip(u u8) -> u8 => -u

fn main() {
    println(flip(200))
}
